        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23019147?u=4c0de81596ced64dc067dea5686f7ca2912db0cb&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I came across the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ToggleEvent\" rel=\"nofollow\">ToggleEvent</a> and <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ToggleEvent/source\" rel=\"nofollow\">ToggleEvent.source</a> pages while reviewing <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41653\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/41653/hovercard\">#41653</a> and noticed few opportunities where the text could be improved and made clearer.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'll leave inline comments to explain some of the specific changes.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41670",
            "title": "Editorial updates to ToggleEvent and ToggleEvent.source pages",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-27T10:39:03.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-25T03:10:19.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "dipikabh",
                "url": "https://github.com/dipikabh"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">text-decoration-trim</code> property is supported behind a preference as of Firefox 145. See <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979915\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1979915</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've verified that it does work to a degree, although it currently seems buggy. As a result, I don't think we should add docs or BCD for this feature yet, but it does warrant an experimental features entry.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41665",
            "title": "Add text-decoration-trim experimental feature entry",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-27T10:42:43.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-24T14:48:45.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF145 supports CSS module scripts in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1720570\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1720570</a> - i.e. you can import a stylesheet as a module using <code class=\"notranslate\">import</code> and the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Statements/import/with\" rel=\"nofollow\">import attribute</a> <code class=\"notranslate\">type</code> with value  <code class=\"notranslate\">\"css\"</code></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The support is only in preview, and is disabled by default. This adds update to experimental features and to release note.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3510263242\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41503\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41503/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41503\">#41503</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41654",
            "title": "Ff145 Release note for CSS module scripts",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-27T10:42:42.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-24T04:19:04.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #41646.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3544088922\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41646\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41646/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41646\">#41646</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41651",
            "title": "Set-Cookie: Domain directive default value clarification",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-27T09:03:33.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-24T00:12:04.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chromium browsers support <a href=\"https://privacysandbox.google.com/protections/user-agent\" rel=\"nofollow\">User-Agent reduction</a>, which means that features such as the <code class=\"notranslate\">User-Agent</code> HTTP header provide less-specific information in an effort to reduce their effectiveness for fingerprinting/tracking.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds information on User-Agent reduction to appropriate places on MDN, as well as a new guide to cover it, and some extra information on client-side hints.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR is part of the final set of privacy sandbox information to be added to MDN. Much of it is being removed, but this feature is stable and will be kept, so it should be added.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41648",
            "title": "Editorial review: Information about User-Agent reduction",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-26T23:16:16.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-23T14:41:25.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
